Well, because they destroy everything in the right squares when they're
touched in naughty ways ;-)

Seriously -- the most popular instadeath drawbridge is the Castle (I
can't remember if there're other drawbridges in vanilla Quest levels).
While the Castle drawbridge is still up you can be killed:
- while standing in the moat square next to it and playing the
drawbridge tune
- while standing in the moat square next to it and zapping a wand of
striking at it
- while standing in the moat square next to it and zapping a wand of
opening
- while standing in the moat square next to it and casting a spell of
knock

I'm pretty sure I didn't get all of 'em.  The obvious solution here, of
course, is "don't stand in the moat square next to the drawbridge"

Additionally, once the drawbridge is down, a wand of striking zapped at
the bridge will cause it to collapse, killing anyone on top of (or in
the square it started on) it even if you're levitating.  Therefore, if
you get caught on or near the bridge while battling your way into the
castle, a stray soldier with a wand of striking can end your game in a
single turn.

Drawbridges suck.

